{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root-cause investigation (worktree fix-finwhale at 459ad3874dd). (1) With the read-path reconverge throttle marker absent, rebar.comment on a superseded clone SUCCEEDS on current main: emit_cross_session_warning -> show_ticket -> reads.ensure_fresh -> sync.reconverge runs the stale-clone override before finalize_event. (2) With the marker stamped as just-run (a read in the last 60 s, the normal state of a busy MCP server), the same write is refused as DIVERGED. That is the CLI/MCP difference. (3) Experiment: making write_blocking_divergence return None when the remote epoch supersedes local lets the write commit, but the event never reaches the remote: push non-FF -> push_recovery merge of the unrelated history fails 5 times ('merge conflict'). So the original Fix section was insufficient; plan revised to also route push recovery through the existing override. Acceptance criteria unchanged."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795233579374003001,"uuid":"827ec5fc-8373-4b53-822a-5fb1d0b7a547"}